Package: lesusa
Title: Stone-Geary (LES) Parameter Database for the United States with
    Exact Aggregation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Thiago", "Simonato", email = "thiago.c.simonato@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Ships the frisch_friedman_v1.3.0-tier2 release of theoretically
    consistent Linear Expenditure System (Stone-Geary) parameters for the
    United States, 2017-2019, on a 51 state x 10 income decile x 5 age grid
    over 42 goods, together with one aggregation function. les_aggregate()
    aggregates goods, regions and household types to any user classification
    exactly at the base point (the aggregated LES reproduces aggregate demand
    with no error and preserves adding-up, Engel aggregation, homogeneity and
    Cournot by construction) and re-derives budget shares and elasticities
    from the closed forms rather than averaging them. An optional
    family-formation axis is composed at call time by biproportional fitting
    (RAS). Output as GEMPACK .har for CGE models or long CSV. Every call
    self-audits and refuses to emit an inconsistent result.
